# Model config: Qwen3.8-27B instruct/non-thinking on Q4 weights -- model-intrinsic.
#
# UD-Q4_K_XL weights (as models/qwen3.8-27b-q4.env) with the INSTRUCT sampling
# recipe (as models/qwen3.8-27b-instruct.env). This pairing exists for the
# single R9700, where Q8 weights leave no room for a KV cache.
#
# Sampling -- INSTRUCT / non-thinking:
#   temp 0.7, top-p 0.80, top-k 20, min-p 0.0, presence 1.5, repeat 1.0
# See models/qwen3.8-27b-instruct.env for why presence-penalty is 1.5 here and
# 0.0 in thinking mode, and for the mandatory caller-side flag:
#   chat_template_kwargs: {"enable_thinking": false}
# Without that flag the model still thinks, and instruct sampling applied to
# thinking output is the worst of both.
#
# Architecture / KV math / vision: see models/qwen3.8-27b.env.

: "${MODEL:=Qwen3.8-27B/Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf}"

LLAMA_ARGS+=(--temp 0.7 --top-p 0.80 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0 --presence-penalty 1.5 --repeat-penalty 1.0)
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--mmproj "/models/Qwen3.8-27B/mmproj-F16.gguf")
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--alias qwen3.8-27b-instruct)
